, and docs for agent_runners[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]host-guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-guard[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]host-guard: teach the Python preflight host to build runner-slot agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]snapshots for the new provider, accept it in `sase.schema.json`, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]document it, and cover it with tests including count parity.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Guard skips stop consuming run_every cadence[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]guard-cadence[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]guard-cadence: stop advancing a chop's `run_every` clock when the skip [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]came from an `inhibit_if` guard rather than from the configured trigger,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so a guarded chop retries on the next tick.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Enable the idle guard on bugyi_chop_ci_watch[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #5FD7AF] xsmall [/bold black on #5FD7AF]\n    [#AF87FF]ci-watch-idle[dim] · [dim][/dim]after host-guard[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ci-watch-idle: add `inhibit_if: {agent_runners: {max: 0}}` to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`ci_watch` chop in the chezmoi-managed config, refresh its description [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]body, and verify the live runtime accepts and honors it.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ko","hidden":false,"llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","phase_bead_id":"sase-ko.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-908a09b503f545da95f35ad39757593a","started_at":"2026-08-12T16:01:17.198027","state":"dismissed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1786567158,"sha":"7e8f528b2f3f235ca7a4e3916af404065b728150","subject":"feat(axe): add age